    {
      "annotations": {
        "destructiveHint": false,
        "idempotentHint": false,
        "openWorldHint": false,
        "readOnlyHint": false
      },
      "description": "Prepare an immutable preview and field diff for 1–8 guest-free changes: a single event, an all-day event, or one occurrence of a recurring series (update or delete=cancel, by the event_ref from agenda; the preview names the series and the occurrence's original start). Series-wide, this-and-following and guest changes are refused with capability_unverified. Only a local plan record is stored for apply; no calendar mutation occurs. Timed event start/end: ISO 8601 with offset, or wall time YYYY-MM-DDTHH:MM[:SS] read in the event's IANA timezone (timezone required). All-day event: all_day=true with start/end as YYYY-MM-DD dates, end exclusive and optional (default start+1 day), no timezone; an occurrence cannot switch between timed and all-day. Advisory cached overlap checks cover visible calendars only. project (event_ref of a lesson occurrence from agenda, calendar_ref of its calendar, activity label of the guardian rules) adds one linked drive per enabled rule of that child and activity into the guardian's Google calendar: drop-off ends at the lesson start, pick-up at its end; the rule's title, the place only if the rule copies it, no description or guests, private when the rule says so. Rules that get no drive are listed in projections_skipped with a reason; nothing_to_project names the activity labels. One project counts as one of the 8 actions; a plan holds at most 16 steps (too_many_steps). unproject (calendar_ref and event_ref of the lesson, or the operation_id of your projecting operation) deletes only drives DeedKit created and that are unchanged since: a drive edited by anyone is a version_conflict and stays, one already gone just closes its link, one whose outcome is unknown is listed in projections_skipped as outcome_unknown (run reconcile first); the lesson itself is never touched. nothing_to_unproject means no live drive is left. With carry_projections (set by the gateway), create with activity adds the new lesson's drives after it (sent only once the lesson create is verified). update or delete of a projected lesson carries its drives in the same plan: each live drive moves by its rule or is deleted, only if unchanged since DeedKit wrote it (else version_conflict, operation partial); drives that cannot follow are listed in projections_skipped (projection_pending, outcome_unknown, target_not_writable, source_all_day). project on a lesson whose drives drifted proposes the fix (reproject: true): a drive of a moved lesson moves to the new span, a drive deleted outside DeedKit is created again; a drive changed by hand is skipped as projection_edited, and a cancelled lesson's drives as use_unproject.",
      "inputSchema": {
        "properties": {
          "actions": {
            "items": {
              "$ref": "#/$defs/Action"
            },
            "maxItems": 8,
            "minItems": 1,
            "title": "Actions",
            "type": "array"
          },
